We want to find the multiplicative inverse of 2 modulo 185.
We can use the extended Euclidean algorithm to find this inverse.
Since $2$ and $185$ are relatively prime, the Euclidean algorithm will terminate in one step.
\begin{align*}
185 &= 92 \cdot 2 + 1 \\
2 &= 2 \cdot 1 + 0
\end{align*}
Hence, $\gcd(2, 185) = 1$, and we can work our way back up to express $\gcd(2, 185)$ as a linear combination of 2 and 185.
\begin{align*}
1 &= 185 - 92 \cdot 2
\end{align*}
Thus, the modular inverse of 2 modulo 185 is $-92 \equiv \boxed{93} \pmod{185}$.The answer is: 93

