Let $x = \operatorname{arccot} \frac{4}{7}.$ Then $\cot x = \frac{4}{7}.$ Taking the reciprocal of both sides gives $\tan x = \frac{7}{4}.$
Therefore, $\tan \left (\operatorname{arccot} \frac{4}{7} \right) = \boxed{\frac{7}{4}}.$
The answer is: \frac{7}{4}

